<title>OMAN: Oman's GDP rises 7.6 percent in first half 1996.</title>
<headline>Oman's GDP rises 7.6 percent in first half 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MUSCAT 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oman's gross domestic product (GDP) at market prices rose 7.6 percent to 2.75 billion rials in the first half of 1996, provisional Ministry of Development figures show.</p>
<p>Contribution to GDP by sectors in millions of rials:</p>
<p>    (figures rounded)			H1 1996	 H1 1995</p>
<p>Petroleum activities</p>
<p> Crude petroleum			     1,076.9	   994.0</p>
<p> Natural gas					22.7	    21.9</p>
<p>Total petroleum activities		 1,099.6	 1,015.9</p>
<p>Non-petroleum activities</p>
<p> Mining and quarrying			    5.7	     5.0</p>
<p> Manufacturing				   123.7	   115.6</p>
<p> Electricity and water			  20.5	    20.3</p>
<p> Building and construction		    43.4	    51.4</p>
<p> Wholesale and retail trade		  351.3	   324.1</p>
<p> Public administration and defence	 374.5	   351.7</p>
<p> Other activities				795.2	   727.6</p>
<p>Total non-petroleum activities	   1,714.4	 1,595.6</p>
<p>Financial intermediation		     (83.8)	  (75.0)</p>
<p>Customs duties				    20.5	    18.9</p>
<p>GDP at market prices			 2,750.7	 2,555.4</p>
</text>
